\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.1}{\ignorespaces Schematic illustration of the two trigonally-warped Fermi surfaces situated at the neighboring valleys, $K_+$ and $K_-$. The hot-spot pairs on each surface, linked by the incommensurate wavevector $\boldsymbol  {Q}$ (depicted by the black arrow), are emphasised. In the $K_+$ ($K_-$) valley, the fermionic degrees of freedom localised near the right and left hot-spots are denoted $\psi _+^{(1)}$ ($\psi _-^{(2)}$) and $\psi _+^{(2)}$ ($\psi _-^{(1)}$), respectively. These fermions interact with the critical cavity-photon modes, which carry momenta centered about $\boldsymbol  {\mathcal  {Q}}$.}}{70}{}\protected@file@percent }
